<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Carrara</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Carrara is a town in northern Tuscany at the foot of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apuan-alps">Apuan Alps</a>, famous for its white marble, quarried since Roman times. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/michelangelo">Michelangelo</a> chose blocks there for his sculptures. Bought by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malaspina">Malaspina</a> in 1473, it formed with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/massa-tuscany">Massa</a> the Duchy of Massa and Carrara until 1829, and its quarries remain among the largest in the world.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/carrara.jpg" alt="Carrara" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sailko · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Carrara,_veduta_verso_il_centro_storico,_avenza_e_il_mare_da_via_salita_sponda_04.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
